## What I did

Added two bullets to the Safety Rules section of CLAUDE.md, right after the run_git() guard:

1. **Never add a definition without its consumer in the same edit** — names all three shapes (fn → call site, let → reader, enum variant → every match), states which gate catches each, gives the escape hatch (inline at the call site instead of dangling), and cites #618/#653/#658/#647 so the rule carries its own evidence.
2. **Run `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` explicitly before declaring a task complete** — with the reason: watch runs mid-turn and skips when nothing changed, so the last edit of a task is the one most likely to be unlinted.

## Verification of the four instances — checked, not assumed

I read the revert issue bodies rather than trusting the table. All four hold, with two corrections worth stating:

• #618 added three dead functions, not one — strip_quoted_regions, `detect_git_redirect, detect_git_redirect_in_tokens`. The table undercounts. (The task file for that retry literally said "WIRE FIRST." It knew the failure mode and still shipped the definition without the call site.)
• #647 is a rustc build error, not a clippy lint. Revert reason reads "Build failed after fix attempt", not "Clippy failed" — E0004 fails earlier and harder than `-D dead-code. I wrote the rule to say so explicitly rather than lumping all four under -D warnings`. A false claim in CLAUDE.md gets re-injected as authoritative context every session (Day 130), so the extra clause was worth its width.

#653 and #658 are exactly as described.

